#: src/types-and-values/solution.md:33
msgid "Panic"
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/solution.md:35
msgid ""
"The exercise asks when this function will panic. The Fibonacci sequence "
"grows very rapidly. With `u32`, the calculated values will overflow the 32-"
"bit integer limit (4,294,967,295) when `n` reaches 48."
msgstr ""

#: src/types-and-values/solution.md:39
msgid ""
"In Rust, integer arithmetic checks for overflow in _debug mode_ (which is "
"the default when using `cargo run`). If an overflow occurs, the program will "
"panic (crash with an error message). In _release mode_ (`cargo run --"
"release`), overflow checks are disabled by default, and the number will wrap "
"around (modular arithmetic), producing incorrect results."
msgstr ""

